.com/story/experts-health-care/SS-2-135539/SS-2-255211/">http://stream.wsj.com/story/experts-health-care/SS-2-135539/SS-2-255211/</ext-link></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B6"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dub&#x000e9;</surname><given-names>L., J.</given-names></name><name><surname>LeBel</surname><given-names>L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Lu</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>2005</year>). <article-title>Affect Asymmetry and Comfort Food Consumption</article-title>, <source>Physiol. Behav</source>. <volume>86</volume>, <fpage>559</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>567</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.physbeh.2005.08.023</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16209880</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B7"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Frank</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Laharnar</surname><given-names>N.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kullmann</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Veit</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Canova</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Preissl</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>2010</year>). <article-title>Processing of food pictures: influence of hunger, gender and calorie content</article-title>. <source>Brain Res</source>. <volume>1350</volume>, <fpage>159</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>166</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.brainres.2010.04.030</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">20423700</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hamilton</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>1960</year>). <article-title>A rating scale for depression</article-title>. <source>J. Neurol. Neurosurg. Psychiat</source>. <volume>23</volume>, <fpage>56</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>62</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/jnnp.23.1.56</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14399272</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kampov-Polevoy</surname><given-names>A. B.</given-names></name><name><surname>Alterman</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Khalitov</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Garbutt</surname><given-names>J. C.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>2006</year>). <article-title>Sweet preference predicts mood altering effect of and impaired control over eating sweet foods</article-title>. <source>Eat Behav</source>. <volume>7</volume>, <fpage>181</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>187</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.eatbeh.2005.09.005</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16843219</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nestler</surname><given-names>E. J.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>2012</year>). <article-title>Epigenetics: stress makes its molecular mark</article-title>. <source>Nature</source><volume>490</volume>, <fpage>171</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>172</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/490171a</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">23060173</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><mixed-citation publication-type="webpage"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Organization for Economic Co-operation and Development</collab></person-group> (<year>OECD, 2011</year>). <source>Family Database: Life Expectancy at Birth</source>. Available online at: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.oecd.org/els/family/CO1.2%20Life%20expectancy%20at%20birth%20-%20updated%20081212.pdf">http://www.oecd.org/els/family/CO1.2%20Life%20expectancy%20at%20birth%20-%20updated%20081212.pdf</ext-link></mixed-citat